# The guard of joins() fails on a parsed record, so its slow version runs, and that believes nothing of `parts`. It ran the whole protocol in every turn: a call of next(), a look for `done`, a look for `value`: 266 instructions a turn,
# where the same body without a guard takes 108. A body that knows nothing of what it iterates asks it in front of the loop whether it is a list as made and goes by index where it is, with the protocol as the other way: a question
# that the code itself asks is no belief, so the loop of a slow version asks it too. Nothing there is proven: the element is read as one that is expected, and of what it is nothing is said.
# f1 = joins
# RUN(SLOW): walk f1:SlowBody mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(SLOW): as-written
# SLOW: IsPristine {{*}} builtinClass=Array
# SLOW: GetArrayElement {{*}} level=Expected
# SLOW-NOT: level=Proven
# SLOW-NOT: CheckProof
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = () => {};
